{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787370965268669001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"solid-velour-lynx","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"1f0c8df8de6c8f082cb8be1b04a68dac0d5e36ef4022ff3a823dff50779d3e8e","event_uuid":"686f5350-ffca-4847-aced-ee1343772816","position":{"commit_sha":"beae050d99ae7e678db8bc9af56f68786fd946dc","position":"1787367500844204001-686f5350-ffca-4847-aced-ee1343772816"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"1aced9fd86ea950b8e2384e4cee04288ced6b7c0009f3ee1d66b4ac8f135959f","event_uuid":"4e2351a2-bacb-4731-9264-d3f25c03e130","position":{"commit_sha":"b14146dccac66b9ee97b29a4638be61a39019180","position":"1787367531259403001-4e2351a2-bacb-4731-9264-d3f25c03e130"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787367500844204001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"4e2351a2-bacb-4731-9264-d3f25c03e130","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"58bd-d656-c52f-4cf4"}],"description":"## Problem\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_ensures.py::test_mcp_startup_sweeps_before_run` fails intermittently under CI's pytest-randomly (observed on a py3.13 shard: assertion `order == ['ensures','run']` got `['run']`, i.e. run_ensures was never called). It passes in isolation and on other py-version shards (different random seed).\n\n## Root cause\n`mcp_server.main()` only calls `run_ensures` when `os.path.isdir(_config.tracker_dir())` (src/rebar/mcp_server.py ~line 717). Under an unlucky test order a sibling test leaves cwd / tracker-dir resolution state such that `tracker_dir()` does not point at an existing dir, so the ensures sweep is silently skipped and only 'run' is recorded. The test relies on ambient cwd/config state the `repo` fixture does not fully isolate.\n\n## Fix direction\nMake the test hermetic (chdir into / point config at the fixture's repo within the test, or assert the tracker-dir precondition) OR make main()'s sweep decision independent of ambient cwd. Root-cause the isolation leak; do not paper over with a retry.\n\n## Impact\nNot caused by RP-06 code_review/plan_review changes — surfaced while landing RP-06 S3 (change 2047); the failing test is disjoint from those files. Pre-existing latent flake on main affecting concurrent sessions.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"de95-1594-1056-436e","ticket_type":"bug","title":"test_fsck_ensures::test_mcp_startup_sweeps_before_run is order-dependent (flaky under pytest-randomly)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["686f5350-ffca-4847-aced-ee1343772816","4e2351a2-bacb-4731-9264-d3f25c03e130"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787370965268669001,"uuid":"3597398c-26f9-4de0-a7d4-2d7e58901869"}